<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115792" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψόγος</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψέγω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>blamable fault, blemish, flaw,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνευ ψόγου τετυγμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					5.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>blame, censure,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνείδεα καὶ ψ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Xenoph.
					11.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοτεινὸς ψ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					7.61
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ τὸν ἀνθρώπειον αἰδεσθῇ ψόγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					937
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				94
			</span></i>: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ ψόγοισι δεννάσεις ἐμέ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					759
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ ψιλῶ ψόγους κλύειν</span>
			cj. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψόφους</span> in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				630
			</span></i>; also in Com. and Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				146
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				895
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς πέλας ψ. ἐπενεγκεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.70
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.45
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψ. φέρειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					182a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψ. ἔχειν</span>”
				<i>to be blamed,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					823b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψ. ἀμουσίας ὑφέξοντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					403c
				</span></i>
			: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκώμιά τε καὶ ψόγους ποιεῖν
					ἀλλήλοις</span>”
				<i>lampoons,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					829c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Grg.</u>
				483c
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1448b27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ . . κάλλος καὶ ψ. πολλῶν γέμει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					703
				</span></i>
			:—c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλγος σοί, ψ. δὲ σῷ πατρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					987
				</span></i>
			.</div>
